    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.local_reaching_centrality - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.local_reaching_centrality.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.local_reaching_centrality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate the local reaching centrality of every node.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.local_reaching_centrality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate the local reaching centrality of every node.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.local_reaching_centrality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Calculate the local reaching centrality of every node.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCalculate the local reaching centrality of every node.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L55450-L55566){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.local_reaching_centrality(\n    weighted=None,\n    normalized=True,\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Local reaching centrality](../assets/graphs/local-reaching-centrality.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A five-node directed out-tree, like an org chart: A heads B and C, and B heads D and E. Each node is shaded by the share of the other four nodes it can reach. A reaches all of them and scores 1.00, B reaches D and E for 0.50, and the leaves C, D and E reach no one and score 0.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nLocal reaching centrality (Mones, Vicsek & Vicsek, 2012) measures how much of the\nnetwork a node can reach, and how easily:\n\n- on an unweighted directed graph, it is the share of other nodes reachable from the\n  node, which separates sources at the top of a hierarchy from sinks at the bottom\n- on an unweighted undirected graph, it averages `1 / distance` over all other nodes\n  (unreachable ones count 0), like a normalized harmonic centrality\n- on a weighted graph, it averages the mean edge weight along the strongest path to each\n  reachable node, where strong edges count as short (distance = total weight / weight)\n\nIt is the building block of `global_reaching_centrality()`, which measures how\nhierarchical the whole network is. Values match NetworkX, which computes one node at a\ntime. With weights, if several equally strong paths reach a node, their mean weights can\ndiffer, and the two libraries may pick different ones.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to use edge weights. If `None` (default), follows the graph. Weights must be\n    positive.\n\n<code>[normalized]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   With weights, divide by the mean edge weight so scores are comparable across graphs.\n    Default is `True`. Ignored without weights.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute to store scores in. If `None` (default), uses\n    `\"local_reaching_centrality\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    scores as a node attribute and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, float], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: a dictionary mapping node IDs to scores. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph has fewer than two nodes or no edges, or a weight is not positive.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~global_reaching_centrality`) \n\n:   Summarize the scores as one hierarchy score.\n\n[](`~harmonic_centrality`) \n\n:   Equal up to scale on undirected, unweighted graphs.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIn a reporting tree, the head of the organization reaches everyone and each leaf reaches\nno one:\n\n::: {#a5453937 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\norg = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"ceo\", \"cto\"), (\"ceo\", \"cfo\"), (\"cto\", \"dev1\"), (\"cto\", \"dev2\")],\n    directed=True,\n)\n\norg.local_reaching_centrality().get_node_df().select(\n    \"label\", \"local_reaching_centrality\"\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (5, 2)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>local_reaching_centrality</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;ceo&quot;</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;cto&quot;</td><td>0.5</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;cfo&quot;</td><td>0.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;dev1&quot;</td><td>0.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;dev2&quot;</td><td>0.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Courses that open doors\n\nIn `courses()`, each edge points from a prerequisite to a course that requires it, so a\ncourse's local reaching centrality is the share of the other courses that need it,\ndirectly or through a chain of prerequisites, stored here as `\"reach\"`. Introduction to\nProgramming (CS101) leads to 11 of the other 16, and Data Structures (CS102) to 10:\n\n::: {#ea3f55da .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses = (\n    ec.courses()\n    .local_reaching_centrality(attr_name=\"reach\")\n    .layout_multipartite(subset_key=\"level\")\n)\n\n(\n    courses.get_node_df()\n    .select(\"label\", \"title\", \"reach\")\n    .sort(\"reach\", descending=True)\n    .head(5)\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (5, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>title</th><th>reach</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;CS101&quot;</td><td>&quot;Introduction to Programming&quot;</td><td>0.6875</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;CS102&quot;</td><td>&quot;Data Structures&quot;</td><td>0.625</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;MATH101&quot;</td><td>&quot;Calculus I&quot;</td><td>0.375</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;MATH102&quot;</td><td>&quot;Calculus II&quot;</td><td>0.3125</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;MATH210&quot;</td><td>&quot;Linear Algebra&quot;</td><td>0.25</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWith the courses in columns by number, the scores fall from left to right, and the\n400-level courses, which lead nowhere, score 0:\n\n::: {#a54a3b3a .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses.plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"reach\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-975840b8:#86b6ef;--ect-d37859ca:#6f9ed6;--ect-3922f8c5:#4e7ab2;--ect-e8641f36:#7aaae3;--ect-05c74c51:#6492ca;--ect-6425850a:#0d366b;--ect-0a889086:#184176;--ect-de17e7ab:#426da5;--ect-e76ae989:#5986be;--ect-f8094ac6:#79a8e1;--ect-472663e1:#6d9bd3;--ect-6826a5f9:#608ec6;--ect-9d43aea2:#5480b8;--ect-5ee57d66:#4874ab;--ect-3c980f0e:#3c679e;--ect-ec386ef0:#305a91;--ect-97f76ec5:#254e84;--ect-e28c6970:#194278;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-6970a796:#5d7fa7;--ect-5939a1ab:#4d6e95;--ect-20ecc71d:#36557c;--ect-d9de3ed7:#55769e;--ect-02692b80:#46668d;--ect-bf50105f:#09254a;--ect-5ed30c34:#102d52;--ect-88c21ad6:#2e4c73;--ect-65262fae:#3e5d85;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-975840b8:#184f95;--ect-d37859ca:#3a69a8;--ect-3922f8c5:#6990c3;--ect-e8641f36:#2a5c9e;--ect-05c74c51:#4a76b1;--ect-6425850a:#cde2fb;--ect-0a889086:#bcd4f2;--ect-de17e7ab:#7b9fce;--ect-e76ae989:#5983ba;--ect-f8094ac6:#2c5d9f;--ect-472663e1:#3d6caa;--ect-6826a5f9:#4f7ab4;--ect-